# Line endings are LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This is not a style preference. A CRLF that reaches a `run: |` block in a workflow puts a
# carriage return at the end of every shell line, and bash answers with
# `$'\r': command not found` — a failure whose cause is invisible in the diff that caused
# it, because a carriage return looks like nothing. It got in exactly once, when a script
# rewrote three workflow files on a Windows machine and Python helpfully translated the
# newlines on the way out. core.autocrlf is false here, so git committed them verbatim and
# a thirty-line change arrived as seven hundred.
#
# Same family as the U+2028 that once ended a JSONL line early inside a JSON string. An
# invisible character that changes how a file parses is the kind of defect this repository
# is about, and it deserves a guard rather than a habit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, declared rather than detected. git's heuristic reads NUL bytes and would get
# every one of these right; saying so anyway costs one line each and removes the question.
*.gz binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
*.onnx binary
